  "_purpose": "Labelled EXTENSION set. NOT part of the frozen corpus and never merged into its numbers.",
  "_method": "Authored 2026-08-26, BLIND - written before any line of the extraction cascade existed, so no pattern here was chosen after seeing what the matcher does or does not catch. Committed in that state before the matcher was written; see git history.",
  "_what_it_measures": "Extraction logic against names the frozen corpus does not contain: accented Latin capitals, Vietnamese tone marks, mixed case, and a hyphenated compound surname. Santa Clara County is heavily Latino and Vietnamese, and a corpus of ten unaccented all-caps names overstates recipient_name accuracy for exactly the households this app exists for.",
  "_what_it_does_NOT_measure": "OCR. These are clean hand-authored lines with hand-authored boxes, not photographs. The OCR ceiling is 100% by construction. A number from this set is a claim about the parser and about nothing else, and it must never be quoted beside or merged with the photographed figure.",
  "_geometry": "Boxes are normalised 0-1, top-left origin, matching ExtractionInput. The right-hand metadata column is deliberately interleaved into reading order between the address lines, which is what a real recogniser does and what breaks index-based address walks.",
